Z||000004||william_thorniii||12-22-2000||11:27 AM||||Dad,<P>The cool thing about the I.R. pyrometer is that it will be useful when at the track.  Those typically run around $100-$150 but I am not sure how accurate they will be.  <P>My plans are to purchase the $200 package, an I.R. lamp (from elsewhere), and use a thermocouple to determine the temperatures.  I will probably buy a racing tire temp thermocouple so I can have exact tire temps.  LMK how the I.R. lamp they supply you with works out O.K.?<P>Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
