Z||000010||william_thorniii||12-28-2000||08:45 AM||||DXR,<P>I want the capability of coating my entire cradle.  I could build an oven, but I think that would be overkill.  I am planning on just buying an IR heater from McMaster-Carr or Harbor Frieght, etc.  I will forego the thermocouple for now.  They say that you can see the paint cure when it reaches temp.  And the IR, if positioned correctly will aid in warming me in the garage... as long as I don't move much... yeah right.  I do think that it would be a better investment just to buy the deluxe kit and a separate IR heater.  I had originally planned on the purchase of a used oven for the garage, but then decided that I couldn't fit many of the parts that I would want to do in an oven anyway.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000011||william_thorniii||12-28-2000||08:47 AM||||Black88,<P>The advantage of powder coating over painting is that it is virtually indestructable.  Paint chips, scratches and is not happy being flexed (i.e. on springs) while powder is extremely resilient and pliable.  Yes it will provide an excellent rust barrier as well.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
